{"id": "df391e7f-7fdc-4362-9231-d4e88e35dcfe", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:04:41.120823", "source": "agent", "parent_id": null, "system_prompt": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Collaborate with the researcher to develop an experiment design for the original task. First inspect the masked repository and supplied inputs, then use end_researcher_turn with stage=plan to propose an approach, consequential choices and uncertainties. Wait for explicit researcher approval before developing the full design. After approval, hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer, supported by rationale, controls, feasible checks and repository observations in evidence. State assumptions separately from fixed task requirements. No executed experiment or invented outcome is required for this design-only task. Use inspect_repository and execute_check for exploration. Share concrete findings: private tool output is not automatically sent to the researcher. Revise when needed; do not invent objections or ambiguities to extend the conversation. The researcher decides when to stop."}, "tools": [{"description": "List a repository directory or read a text file. Paths are relative to the task workspace.", "action_type": "InspectRepositoryAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "InspectRepositoryTool", "title": "inspect_repository"}, {"description": "Run a shell command in the isolated task workspace. Use small exploratory checks before submitting your plan.", "action_type": "ExecuteCheckAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ExecuteCheckTool", "title": "execute_check"}, {"description": "Yield a proposed approach (stage=plan) or completed experiment design (stage=result), with evidence, assumptions and uncertainties. The researcher decides when to finish.", "action_type": "ReviewHandoffAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ReviewHandoffTool", "title": "end_researcher_turn"}], "dynamic_context": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<CURRENT_DATETIME>\nThe current date and time is: 2026-10-23T12:04\n</CURRENT_DATETIME>"}, "kind": "SystemPromptEvent"}
{"id": "0da6afec-0213-4530-84b9-cc2aeb104750", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:04:41.123200", "source": "user", "parent_id": "df391e7f-7fdc-4362-9231-d4e88e35dcfe", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Thanks — before any design work, please do a scoping pass only (no full deliverable yet).\\n\\n1) Inspection: confirm what inputs actually exist for this study. The project notes say this is a design-only task with no repository, dataset, or GPU access, so please verify (e.g. list /workspace, note Python/GPU availability) and state explicitly that MathInstruct, Llama 3-70B weights, and any BAdam/LoRA reference implementations are NOT locally available. Do not imply anything was run or downloaded.\\n\\n2) Proposed approach: sketch, at a high level, how you would structure an experimental design that answers the comparison question — BAdam vs LoRA adapters when finetuning Llama 3-70B on MathInstruct, evaluated zero-shot on math benchmarks. I want to see the skeleton you intend to fill in: (a) method definitions and the specific activation/parameter-update sparsity mechanism you will attribute to BAdam, and the LoRA configuration you will treat as the baseline; (b) the fairness/equity axes you plan to control (trainable-parameter budget, update sparsity, optimizer, LR schedule, epochs/steps, data ordering, seed set, precision, context length, batching); (c) the evaluation protocol (which math benchmarks, few-shot vs true zero-shot prompting, answer extraction/scoring, contamination handling); (d) reported cost metrics (memory, tokens/sec, wall-clock, storage/IO) since BAdam's claimed advantage is largely memory/throughput; (e) the statistical analysis plan (seeds, variance, primary vs secondary endpoints, decision rule for \\\"better performance\\\").\\n\\n3) Surface the consequential assumptions and uncertainties you are making, and mark them as assumptions rather than established facts. In particular: what exactly counts as \\\"zero-shot\\\" here; which math benchmarks you would select and why; whether the comparison is parameter-matched or compute-matched; how you handle the possibility that the answer is a null result or a memory-win-but-no-accuracy-win; and any unknowns about resources/runtime budget that would change the design's feasibility.\\n\\nKeep it to a plan and an assumption list — I will review the approach before you write the full design with rationale, controls, analysis plan, and feasibility.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"- **Will BAdam achieve better performance on zero-shot math benchmarks compared to LoRA when finetuning the Llama 3-70B model on the MathInstruct dataset?**\\n\\n\\n- **Will BAdam achieve better performance on zero-shot math benchmarks compared to LoRA when finetuning the Llama 3-70B model on the MathInstruct dataset?**\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
