... Actually the MRD is 0.5pt for the decision rule. Honest approach: define power via a formula: for a paired-proportion difference, needed n ≈ (z_{1-α/2}+z_{1-β})² · p_d / (Δ - MRD?)... Let's set up: we test H0: Δ ≤ MRD (0.5pt) vs H1: Δ > MRD (a \" superiority over MRD\" test). Then needed n = (z_{0.975}+z_{0.8})² · σ_Δ² / δ² where δ = true effect beyond MRD (say the design-detectable difference is 1.5 pt total, so δ = 1.0 pt). With σ_Δ per item = sqrt(p_d) ≈ sqrt(0.2)=0.447 → n = (1.96+0.84)²·0.2/(0.01)² = 7.84·0.2/1e-4 = 15,680 items. That's more than GSM8K+MATH combined (6319). So honest conclusion: the study is powered to detect differences of roughly ≥1.2–1.5 pt on the primary endpoint with the full test sets, and NOT 0.5 pt. This is a genuinely important honesty finding: I should say the pre-registered decision rule with MRD 0.5pt is a *claim-warranting threshold*, not a power claim, and state the actual detectable-effect floor; plus pre-register that if the decontaminated subset falls below a floor (n_min such that half-width ≤ ~1.5 pt for the pooled endpoint), we revert to the full test set with disclosed contamination rates and a sensitivity analysis.\n\nCompute n_min for the pooled endpoint: SE_pooled = 0.5·sqrt(p_d1/n1 + p_d2/n2). Let me do a quick script with realistic assumptions, including overlap-rate triggers (e.g., if flagged fraction > 20% of either test set, or decontaminated n < n_min).\n\n3. Eval cost arithmetic: tokens for eval. MATH 5000 × (prompt ~200 + 1024 output) ≈ 5000×1224 ≈ 6.1M tokens; per-seed per-arm generation, and per model = 2 arms × 3 seeds = 6 trained models (+ base reference). Generation FLOPs ≈ 2·P·tokens(decode) for prefill+decode; decode cost per token ~2P FLOPs. So 6 models × ~10M tokens × 2·70e9 = 6×10e6×1.4e11 = 8.4e18 FLOPs → compared to training 4.7e19/epoch... eval ≈ 0.18 epoch-equivalents per... hmm let me actually compute properly including all benchmarks (MATH 5000, GSM8K 1319, GSM-Hard 1319, SVAMP 1000, MultiArith ~600, MMLU-stem ~1800 (multiple choice, short output), AQuA 254, TheoremQA 800) with few-shot arms tripling some. Then compute node-hours at the same MFU assumption, and note decode MFU is far lower (memory-bandwidth-bound, maybe 25-40% of peak at large batch... actually decode with large batch achieves maybe 30-50% MFU on H100). I'll present as analytic estimates with explicit assumptions and ranges.\n\nLet me compute all of this in one script, and also tier scaling table (8B vs 70B, A100 vs H100).\n\nLet me run the arithmetic.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom math import sqrt\nz=1.96\ndef paired_se(pd,n): return sqrt(pd/n)          # SE of paired proportion diff, per item set\ndef pooled_se(pd_g,n_g,pd_m,n_m):                # endpoint = mean(GSM8K acc, MATH acc)\n    return 0.5*sqrt(pd_g/n_g + pd_m/n_m)\n\nprint(\"=== A. paired-difference SE on FULL test sets (n_g=1319, n_m=5000) ===\")\nfor pd in (0.10,0.20,0.30):\n    se=pooled_se(pd,1319,pd,5000)\n    print(f\" discordance {pd:.2f}: pooled SE={100*se:.2f} pt, item-only 95%CI halfwidth={100*1.96*se:.2f} pt\")\nprint(\"\\n=== B. seed-level term: total SE = sqrt(item_var + s_run^2/k), claim needs Delta_hat > MRD + t(k-1)*SE_run ===\")\nt={2:4.303,3:3.182,4:2.776,5:2.571,6:2.447,8:2.365}\nfor s_run in (0.005,0.01,0.015,0.02):\n    print(f\" run-level SD of pooled endpoint = {100*s_run:.1f} pt\")\n    for k in (3,4,5,7,9):\n        se_seeds=s_run/sqrt(k); half=t[k-1]*se_seeds\n        tot=sqrt(0.0128**2+se_seeds**2)           # item term ~1.28pt at pd=0.2\n        print(f\"   k={k}: CI halfwidth(seeds only, t)={100*half:5.2f} pt | total 95% halfwidth={100*1.96*tot:5.2f} pt | Delta_hat needed to clear 0.5pt MRD={0.5+100*half:5.2f} pt\")\nprint(\"\\n=== C. min decontaminated item counts for the decontaminated-subset analysis ===\")\nfor pd in (0.15,0.20,0.25):\n    row=[]\n    for target_hw in (0.015,0.02,0.025):          # halfwidth targets on pooled endpoint\n        # solve 0.5*sqrt(pd/n*(1319/1319)) style: assume decon keeps same fraction f of both sets\n        # pooled_se with n_g=1319f, n_m=5000f\n        import scipy\n    print(f\" pd={pd}\")\n    for f in (1.0,0.9,0.8,0.7,0.6,0.5,0.4):\n        se=pooled_se(pd,int(1319*f),pd,int(5000*f))\n        print(f\"   retained fraction {f:.1f} (n_g={int(1319*f):5d}, n_m={int(5000*f):5d}): SE={100*se:.2f} pt, 95% halfwidth={100*1.96*se:.2f} pt\")\nPY", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-aae76f9793b9e644", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-aae76f9793b9e644", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom math import sqrt\\nz=1.96\\ndef paired_se(pd,n): return sqrt(pd/n)          # SE of paired proportion diff, per item set\\ndef pooled_se(pd_g,n_g,pd_m,n_m):                # endpoint = mean(GSM8K acc, MATH acc)\\n    return 0.5*sqrt(pd_g/n_g + pd_m/n_m)\\n\\nprint(\\\"=== A. paired-difference SE on FULL test sets (n_g=1319, n_m=5000) ===\\\")\\nfor pd in (0.10,0.20,0.30):\\n    se=pooled_se(pd,1319,pd,5000)\\n    print(f\\\" discordance {pd:.2f}: pooled SE={100*se:.2f} pt, item-only 95%CI halfwidth={100*1.96*se:.2f} pt\\\")\\nprint(\\\"\\\\n=== B. seed-level term: total SE = sqrt(item_var + s_run^2/k), claim needs Delta_hat > MRD + t(k-1)*SE_run ===\\\")\\nt={2:4.303,3:3.182,4:2.776,5:2.571,6:2.447,8:2.365}\\nfor s_run in (0.005,0.01,0.015,0.02):\\n    print(f\\\" run-level SD of pooled endpoint = {100*s_run:.1f} pt\\\")\\n    for k in (3,4,5,7,9):\\n        se_seeds=s_run/sqrt(k); half=t[k-1]*se_seeds\\n        tot=sqrt(0.0128**2+se_seeds**2)           # item term ~1.28pt at pd=0.2\\n        print(f\\\"   k={k}: CI halfwidth(seeds only, t)={100*half:5.2f} pt | total 95% halfwidth={100*1.96*tot:5.2f} pt | Delta_hat needed to clear 0.5pt MRD={0.5+100*half:5.2f} pt\\\")\\nprint(\\\"\\\\n=== C. min decontaminated item cou