{"id": "bbbb3058-0b54-4b59-8384-edd5e18a93d0", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:12:25.751449", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "93a5ef39-8a7b-4c31-ba92-6bee0aba788e", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "Fix the scripts (scipy not available; tot accumulation bug — I added to tot_zero not tot).\n\nKey finding from part A/B: with a pooled endpoint = mean of two benchmark accuracies, the item-level term alone gives 95% half-width ~0.96–1.66 pt, which is LARGER than the 0.5 pt MRD. That's an important honesty point: the MRD of 0.5 pt on the pooled endpoint is below the item-level noise floor unless arms are highly concordant (low discordance). Wait — careful. The paired difference SE depends on discordance pd (fraction of items where arms disagree). If discordance is small (e.g., 5%), SE = 0.5*sqrt(0.05/1319 + 0.05/5000)=0.5*sqrt(3.79e-5+1e-5)=0.5*sqrt(4.79e-5)=0.5*0.00692=0.00346=0.35pt → half-width 0.68pt. So the MRD of 0.5 is achievable only when discordance is ≤ ~8%. Let me compute the max discordance for which the item-level term alone doesn't blow the ±0.5 CI. Also note item-level uncertainty is FIXED regardless of seeds — more seeds don't reduce it. This is a crucial point for the seed-honesty section: total CI is dominated by whichever is larger, and seeds only shrink the run-level term.\n\nLet me redo the computations properly and get the max-discordance threshold and the decontaminated minimum-n numbers.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom math import sqrt\ndef pooled_se(pd_g,n_g,pd_m,n_m): return 0.5*sqrt(pd_g/n_g + pd_m/n_m)\nprint(\"=== A. item-level (paired) term on FULL sets, vs run-level term (seeds) ===\")\nfor pd in (0.05,0.08,0.10,0.20,0.30):\n    se=pooled_se(pd,1319,pd,5000); print(f\" paired discordance {pd:.2f}: item SE={100*se:.2f} pt, 95% halfwidth={100*1.96*se:.2f} pt\")\nprint(\"\\n=== B. decontaminated subsets: retained fraction f of BOTH test sets ===\")\nfor pd in (0.10,0.20):\n    print(f\" discordance {pd}:\")\n    for f in (1.0,0.9,0.8,0.7,0.6,0.5,0.4,0.3):\n        ng,nm=int(1319*f),int(5000*f); se=pooled_se(pd,ng,pd,nm)\n        print(f\"   f={f:.1f}  n_g={ng:5d} n_m={nm:5d} -> SE={100*se:.2f} pt, halfwidth={100*1.96*se:.2f} pt\")\nprint(\"\\n=== C. min n needed for decon analysis to keep halfwidth <= 1.0 pt at pd=0.15 (scaling both sets by f) ===\")\npd=0.15\nfor f in [x/100 for x in range(100,19,-1)]:\n    se=pooled_se(pd,int(1319*f),pd,int(5000*f))\n    if 1.96*se<=0.010:\n        print(f\" first f meeting <=1.0pt: f={f:.2f} -> n_g={int(1319*f)}, n_m={int(5000*f)}, halfwidth={100*1.96*se:.2f} pt\"); break\nfor f in [x/100 for x in range(100,19,-1)]:\n    se=pooled_se(pd,int(1319*f),pd,int(5000*f))\n    if 1.96*se<=0.015:\n        print(f\" first f meeting <=1.5pt: f={f:.2f} -> n_g={int(1319*f)}, n_m={int(5000*f)}, halfwidth={100*1.96*se:.2f} pt\"); break\nprint(\"\\n=== D. seed-count sizing: detectable Delta_hat (pooled endpoint) to clear MRD=0.5pt ===\")\nt={3:4.303,4:3.182,5:2.776,6:2.571,7:2.447,9:2.365}\nfor s in (0.008,0.012,0.020):\n    print(f\" assumed run-level SD s_run={100*s:.1f} pt:\")\n    for k in (3,4,5,7,9):\n        hw_seeds=t[k-1]*s/sqrt(k); hw_tot=1.96*sqrt((0.0069)**2+(s/sqrt(k))**2)\n        print(f\"   k={k}: seed-term halfwidth={100*hw_seeds:4.2f} pt | total halfwidth={100*hw_tot:4.2f} pt | detectable Delta_hat={0.5+100*hw_seeds:4.2f} pt\")\nprint(\"\\n=== E. cost arithmetic (analytic) ===\")\nP70,P8=70e9,8e9\nsets={\"MATH test\":(5000,250,1024),\"GSM8K\":(1319,200,1024),\"GSM-Hard\":(1319,250,1024),\"SVAMP\":(1000,200,512),\n      \"MultiArith\":(600,200,512),\"MMLU-math\":(1800,300,16),\"AQuA\":(254,300,16),\"TheoremQA\":(800,350,1024)}\ndef gf(it,p,o,P=P70): return it*(2*P*p+2*P*o)\ntot=sum(gf(*v) for v in sets.values())\nprim=gf(5000,250,1024)+gf(1319,200,1024)\nfull=tot+2*prim\nprint(f\" zero-shot battery, 1 model = {tot/1e18:.3f}e18 FLOP ; +4&8-shot on primaries = {full/1e18:.3f}e18\")\nM=2*3+1\nprin