{"id": "c37efb97-182b-4929-9a7a-e579be432262", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:23:26.873939", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "65e63b9a-7e30-4b2a-9301-a13d128f0878", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "I need to include answer and evidence. Let me write the full deliverable now. Long answer. Let me compose carefully and completely.\n\nStructure of the answer:\n\n# Design document\n0. Status & provenance\n1. Question, hypotheses, endpoints\n2. Methods: arms and configurations (parameter definitions, block ratio grid, LoRA config, fidelity probe as hard gate)\n3. Controls / equity axes table\n4. Data & preprocessing, contamination protocol with pre-registered power floor and fallback rule\n5. Evaluation protocol (zero-shot definition, scoring, extraction failures, few-shot sensitivity)\n6. Cost metrics (descriptive, first-class)\n7. Statistical analysis plan (estimator, seeds + detectable-effect arithmetic + adaptive sizing rule, decision rules for primary and co-primary secondary, quadrant scheme, multiplicity)\n8. Feasibility: tiered structure with gates and arithmetic table\n9. Results/reporting template\n10. Assumption A-list with break-mode column\n11. External validity note (Instruct)\n12. Citation defensibility statement\n13. Preregistration artifact list\n\nEvidence section: environment observations + all arithmetic outputs.\n\nNumbers to use (all labelled analytic):\n- Training: 240k×700 = 1.68e8 tok/epoch; 4·P·T = 4.704e19 FLOPs per 70B epoch = 47.04 e18.\n- 8xA100 (312e12 peak, MFU .35): train 3 seeds×2 arms = 2*3*47.04e18/(8*312e12*.40)... wait my script used mf_t=.35 for A100? I passed .35 for A100 and .40 for H100. Output: 8xA100 k=3: train 89.7 node-h, eval 12.4, total 102.2; k=5: train 149.6, eval 19.6, total 169.1. 8xH100 k=3: train 24.8, eval 3.9, total 28.7; k=5: 41.3/6.2/47.5.\n- Eval battery per model: zero-only 1.757e18 FLOP; with 4&8-shot primaries 3.993e18; 7 models = 27.95e18 ≈ 0.59 of one 70B epoch. Generated tokens: 9.49M/model zero-shot; 22.43M with few-shot; 0.157B across 7 models; at aggregate 1000 tok/s/GPU×8 → 5.5 node-h. Note discrepancy between the two eval estimates (FLOPs-with-MFU-0.25 gives 12.4 node-h on A100, token-rate gives 5.5 on 8 GPUs at 1000 tok/s) → present as a range 1.4–12.4 node-h depending on GPU class and serving efficiency, i.e., eval is 12–14% of total but up to ~30-50% if serving is memory-bound at low MFU. Let me be careful and honest: I'll give both estimates and a range.\n- Note: decode is memory-bandwidth-bound; MFU for decode of a 70B model is far below training MFU (my assumption 0.25 is generous; at 0.1 it'd be ~3x). Let me present: eval 3.9–12.4 node-h (H100/A100 class) under a 0.25 MFU decode assumption; at a more pessimistic 0.10 decode MFU it is 9.8–31 node-h, i.e. eval can rival 1/3 of training cost. Let me quickly compute: A100 eval at MFU .25 = 12.4; at .10 = 31.0; H100 at .25=3.9, at .10=9.8. Yes.\n- 8B pilot: 2.83 node-h training + 0.20 eval on 8xH100 → ~3 node-h. That's the stage-0 cost.\n- 70B/8B ratio 8.75x.\n- Storage: 70B bf16 = 140 GB; r=16 adapter 417 MB bf16; +fp32 master & moments = 2.5 GB. Full checkpoint per run if we save optimizer: ~2.9 GB plus base weights if unsharded copies. For 70B: also note eval serving needs 140GB weights → 2 nodes of 8×80GB for a single replica at bf16 without quantization, or 1 node with FP8/4-bit. That's a real constraint: 8×80GB = 640GB, so 140GB weights fits fine on one node (18GB/GPU sharded), serving on one 8-GPU node is fine.\n- LoRA params: r=16 → 207.1M (0.296%), r=64 → 828.4M (1.183%). Adam fp32 moments at r=64 = 6.63 GB; at 1/8 active = 0.83 GB.\n- Power: item-level paired SE on pooled endpoint (mean of two accuracies) = 0.5*sqrt(pd/ng+pd/nm); at pd=0.10 → 0.49pt, halfwidth 0.96pt; pd=0.20 → 0.69/1.36; pd=0.30 → 0.85/1.66. So the item term alone (≈1.0–1.7 pt) already exceeds the ±0.5 pt MRD. This is a crucial honesty finding: the design as specified (MRD 0.5 pt) cannot be resolved by item-level sampling noise alone